Modifications to the original work (GPL-3.0, section 5a):

2026-11-11  Stage 1: name and branding (DipAlert), Docker image published
            to GitHub Container Registry, TrueNAS deployment file, Polish
            locale, database backups (nightly and before migrations),
            indexes on the prices table, removal of the SearXNG product
            search and of notification channels other than e-mail
            (ntfy, Gotify, Discord, Apprise, Telegram, Pushover),
            first user's password no longer printed to logs.
2026-11-12  Stage 2: fetch layer with FlareSolverr as a store fetch method,
            guard against addresses in the home network (also after
            redirects and for AI provider addresses), per-store interval
            between requests and a growing pause after a block, fetch
            outcome classification, no immediate retries after a block,
            delayed retries only after network errors, AI repair only
            when a page has no price (in the background when started from
            the panel) and never switching a store's fetch method,
            alternating store order in runs, Morele structured data fix.
2026-11-12  Stage 3: notification on a price change from the previous read
            (percent or amount, direction), at most one e-mail per new
            price, price alerts sent through the queue with retries, a
            record of every fetch attempt with the page of a failed one,
            runs as job batches, "Problems" page, daily status e-mail,
            per-product failure e-mails off by default.
2026-11-12  Stage 4: price chart with a store filter and a period (saved
            per product), a 20-colour palette, the lowest price line from
            the chosen stores only, store logos (fetched from the home
            page or uploaded; PNG, JPEG, ICO, WebP only) shown in the panel
            and embedded in e-mails.
